  "description": {
    "main": "Catalogue of Mike Kelley's 2009 Gagosian show of painting, with a conversation between Kelley and Ralph Rugoff.",
    "extended": "<p>The catalogue for <em>Horizontal Tracking Shots</em>, Mike Kelley's first New York exhibition devoted entirely to painting.</p>\n<p class=\"mt-6\">The show ran at Gagosian, 555 West 24th Street, from November 7 to December 23, 2009. It combined large multi-part polychrome panels with smaller framed canvases, among them <em>Dark Swallower of Souls</em>, <em>Mort's Mouth</em> and <em>Horizontal Tracking Shot of a Cross Section of Trauma Rooms</em>. The book is mostly plates and includes a dialogue between Kelley and Ralph Rugoff. Mark Francis edited it, and Lorraine Wild and Victor Hu designed it. It has 139 pages.</p>\n<p class=\"mt-6\">Kelley (1954&ndash;2012) said the paintings grew out of his <em>Extracurricular Activity Projective Reconstruction</em> series, in which he treated stage sets as paintings. The panels draw on sources such as textbook illustration, comic strips, science fiction and Modernist abstraction.</p>",
